    "table csv": "Table I. Chemical Compositions of the Experimental Alloys Used in Present Work\n\nAlloys*,Cu,Mg,Fe,Si,Mn,Ti,Al\nB11,4.64,0.27,0.14,0.12,0.12,0.21,bal\nB33,4.61,0.29,0.16,0.29,0.32,0.21,bal\n311,4.66,0.27,0.30,0.11,0.12,0.19,bal\n333,4.62,0.28,0.29,0.29,0.33,0.19,bal\n511,4.69,0.29,0.51,0.11,0.11,0.20,bal\n515,4.68,0.29,0.49,0.09,0.51,0.18,bal\n533,4.64,0.28,0.49,0.30,0.32,0.19,bal\n\nTable III. Tensile Properties of Experimental Alloys in T4 and T7 Conditions\n\nTemper,Properties,B11,B33,311,333,511,515,533\nT4,UTS (MPa),387.1,399.8,364.9,393.2,334.1,353.1,362.5\nT4,YS (MPa),263.6,274.1,260.7,269.7,258.7,259.6,261.9\nT4,El (pct),17.4,9.2,5.5,12.1,3.8,7.5,7.8\nT7,UTS (MPa),454.1,461.1,424.9,450.3,379.4,402.5,423.8\nT7,YS (MPa),413.4,423.3,403.4,426.9,321.3,362.6,384.2\nT7,El (pct),6.2,1.3,1.2,3.1,1.7,2.1,2.8",
    "extracted text": "The paper investigates Al-Cu 206 cast alloys with varying iron contents (0.15-0.5 wt%) and different levels of Mn and Si to evaluate the effect of iron-rich intermetallics on tensile properties. The alloys are designated with codes where the first digit stands for the approximate content of Fe (B for baseline at 0.15 pct Fe), and the second and third digits stand for Si and Mn contents, respectively. The alloys underwent T4 (solution treatment and natural aging) and T7 (solution treatment and artificial overaging) heat treatments. The solution treatment was performed at 793K (520°C) for 8 hours, followed by water quenching at 338K (65°C). For T4, the samples were naturally aged at room temperature for 7 days. For T7, the samples were artificially aged at 458K (185°C) for 5 hours. The paper identifies that the alloys' microstructures contain different types of iron-rich intermetallics (platelet β-Fe or Chinese script α-Fe) depending on composition.",
    "property mapping": "UTS (MPa) -> Ultimate Tensile Strength (MPa)\nYS (MPa) -> Yield Strength (MPa)\nEl (pct) -> Elongation percentage\nT4 -> Solution treatment and natural aging\nT7 -> Solution treatment and artificial overaging",
    "abbreviations": "B11, B33, 311, 333, 511, 515, 533 are alloy designations where the first digit stands for the approximate content of Fe (B for baseline at a maximum specification limit of 0.15 pct Fe). The second and third digits stand for Si and Mn contents, respectively.\nbal -> balance (remainder of composition is aluminum)\npct -> percent\nβ-Fe -> Platelet iron-rich intermetallic phase\nα-Fe -> Chinese script iron-rich intermetallic phase",
